1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,115
早上好，我是鲸鱼娘，今天是10月5日。
Good morning, I'm Whale Girl. Today is October 5.

2
00:00:08,135 --> 00:00:11,465
今天说八件事：Gemini 免费版只剩 Flash-Lite，
Eight stories today: Gemini's free tier drops to Flash-Lite,

3
00:00:11,485 --> 00:00:13,205
德国开源模型 Kolibri，
Germany's open model Kolibri,

4
00:00:13,225 --> 00:00:16,325
DeepSeek Harness 试着兼容 Claude Code 插件，
DeepSeek Harness tries Claude Code plugins,

5
00:00:16,345 --> 00:00:20,005
GPT-6 Astra 打星际输了直接搬顶尖程序，
GPT-6 Astra loses at StarCraft and grabs a top bot,

6
00:00:20,025 --> 00:00:24,025
谷歌暂停开源漏洞赏金，COSMIC 拒收 AI 写的代码，
Google pauses an open-source bug bounty, COSMIC rejects AI-written code,

7
00:00:24,045 --> 00:00:26,605
Gboard 把训练搬进加密服务器，
Gboard moves training into secure servers,

8
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:29,275
还有谷歌治 AI 刷题的新方法。
and Google's new fix for AI that memorizes its tests.

9
00:00:29,295 --> 00:00:31,305
第一件，不付钱的 Gemini 用户，
First, Gemini users who don't pay

10
00:00:31,325 --> 00:00:34,625
这周五起只能用最小的模型 Flash-Lite 了。
will only get the smallest model, Flash-Lite, starting this Friday.

11
00:00:34,645 --> 00:00:36,771
9to5Google 10 月 3 日报道，
9to5Google reported on October 3

12
00:00:36,791 --> 00:00:40,811
谷歌改了 Gemini 应用的模型权限，10 月 9 日起生效。
that Google changed which models the Gemini app offers, starting October 9.

13
00:00:40,831 --> 00:00:45,321
以前免费用户能用 3.6 Flash，3.1 Pro 也能用一部分。
Before, free users had 3.6 Flash and some access to 3.1 Pro.

14
00:00:45,341 --> 00:00:48,026
以后这两个都没了，只剩 Flash-Lite。
Now both are gone, leaving only Flash-Lite.

15
00:00:48,046 --> 00:00:50,721
每月 4.99 美元的 AI Plus 也被砍了一刀：
The $4.99-a-month AI Plus plan gets cut too:

16
00:00:50,741 --> 00:00:53,061
能用 Flash，不能用 Pro。
it keeps Flash but loses Pro.

17
00:00:53,081 --> 00:00:56,583
想要全部三个模型，得订每月 19.99 美元的 AI Pro，
To get all three models, you need AI Pro at $19.99 a month,

18
00:00:56,603 --> 00:00:58,467
或者更贵的 AI Ultra。
or the pricier AI Ultra.

19
00:00:58,487 --> 00:01:01,601
白用的午餐，越来越小份了。
The free lunch keeps getting smaller.

20
00:01:01,801 --> 00:01:07,141
第二件，一个 78B 参数的模型，每处理一个词只动用 3.46B。
Second, a 78B-parameter model that only uses 3.46B for each token.

21
00:01:07,161 --> 00:01:11,612
10 月 3 日，德国 AI 公司 Aleph Alpha 发布了 Kolibri，
On October 3, German AI company Aleph Alpha released Kolibri,

22
00:01:11,632 --> 00:01:12,756
英语和德语双语。
an English-German model.

23
00:01:12,776 --> 00:01:14,926
怎么做到的？混合专家结构，
How? It's a mixture of experts:

24
00:01:14,946 --> 00:01:18,596
每层 384 个专家，每次只挑 6 个干活。
384 experts per layer, with only 6 picked for each token.

25
00:01:18,616 --> 00:01:22,226
权重放在 Hugging Face，用 Apache 2.0 许可。
The weights are on Hugging Face under the Apache 2.0 license.

26
00:01:22,246 --> 00:01:26,466
训练用了 768 块 B200，预训练读了 20T token。
Training used 768 B200 GPUs, with 20T tokens of pre-training.

27
00:01:26,486 --> 00:01:29,864
其中德语超过五分之一，约 4.3T。
German makes up more than a fifth of that, about 4.3T tokens.

28
00:01:29,884 --> 00:01:30,194
官方称，
Aleph Alpha says

29
00:01:30,214 --> 00:01:34,294
它能打平 Nemotron 3 Super 这类激活参数更多的模型，
it matches models with more active parameters, like Nemotron 3 Super.

30
00:01:34,314 --> 00:01:36,184
这是厂商自己的说法。
That's its own claim.

31
00:01:36,204 --> 00:01:39,575
大模型不一定要大算力，省着用也是本事。
A big model doesn't have to burn big compute. Using less is a skill too.

32
00:01:39,775 --> 00:01:42,285
第三件，DeepSeek 的智能体工具 Harness，
Third, DeepSeek's agent tool Harness

33
00:01:42,305 --> 00:01:44,905
开始试着跑 Claude Code 的插件了。
has started trying to run Claude Code plugins.

34
00:01:44,925 --> 00:01:49,322
10 月 3 日，DeepSeek 在 GitHub 上发了 v0.2.1-alpha.1，
On October 3, DeepSeek posted v0.2.1-alpha.1 on GitHub

35
00:01:49,342 --> 00:01:50,588
是个预发布版。
as a pre-release.

36
00:01:50,608 --> 00:01:52,553
上周我们讲过它出了桌面版，
Last week we covered its desktop app.

37
00:01:52,573 --> 00:01:56,443
这次新加的是一个实验性的 Claude Code Mods 兼容层。
This time it adds an experimental Claude Code Mods compatibility layer.

38
00:01:56,463 --> 00:01:58,423
官方说，这步主要是验证：
DeepSeek says this step mainly checks

39
00:01:58,443 --> 00:02:01,833
Claude Code Mods 的能力，大致是 Harness 插件的子集。
that Claude Code Mods' abilities are roughly a subset of Harness plugins.

40
00:02:01,853 --> 00:02:05,073
36氪报道，Token Weather、Blast Radius、
36Kr reports that Token Weather, Blast Radius

41
00:02:05,093 --> 00:02:07,546
Replay Theater 三个示例能跑。
and Replay Theater, three examples, now run.

42
00:02:07,566 --> 00:02:10,157
diff、agents-md 这些还跑不了，
Others like diff and agents-md don't run yet,

43
00:02:10,177 --> 00:02:13,227
官方也说现在还谈不上完整兼容。
and DeepSeek says it isn't full compatibility yet.

44
00:02:13,247 --> 00:02:17,522
另外，插件页加了个入口，可以让 Agent 自己动手做插件。
Also, the plugin page has a new entry that lets the agent build plugins itself.

45
00:02:17,542 --> 00:02:21,157
插件生态谁先做大，别人就得来兼容谁。
Whoever's plugin ecosystem grows first is the one others have to stay compatible with.

46
00:02:21,357 --> 00:02:24,738
第四件，GPT-6 Astra 打《星际争霸》一直输，
Fourth, GPT-6 Astra kept losing at StarCraft,

47
00:02:24,758 --> 00:02:28,781
然后它把人类写的顶尖程序下载下来，替自己上场。
so it downloaded a top bot written by a human and sent that in instead.

48
00:02:28,801 --> 00:02:30,276
Kotaku 10 月 3 日报道，
Kotaku reported on October 3

49
00:02:30,296 --> 00:02:33,276
这事发生在一个叫 StarSkirmish 的比赛里。
that it happened in a competition called StarSkirmish.

50
00:02:33,296 --> 00:02:38,226
规则是：大模型只能用神族，有 1 小时用 C++ 写一个对战程序。
The rules: each model plays only as Protoss and gets 1 hour to write a bot in C++.

51
00:02:38,246 --> 00:02:41,867
Astra 和 Claude Opus 5.5 是 AI 里成绩最好的两个。
Astra and Claude Opus 5.5 are the two best AI competitors.

52
00:02:41,887 --> 00:02:45,797
可 Astra 打不过人类写的程序 Pluto，就去下载了 Stardust。
But Astra couldn't beat Pluto, a human-made bot, so it downloaded Stardust.

53
00:02:45,817 --> 00:02:49,207
Stardust 是 Bruce Mackenzie Nielsen 2020 年写的，
Stardust was written by Bruce Mackenzie Nielsen in 2020.

54
00:02:49,227 --> 00:02:51,016
算是顶尖里的顶尖。
It's one of the very best.

55
00:02:51,036 --> 00:02:52,531
比赛创办人 Kai McPheeters
The competition's creator, Kai McPheeters,

56
00:02:52,551 --> 00:02:55,541
把 Astra 的代码回滚了，让它接着比。
rolled back Astra's code and let it keep playing.

57
00:02:55,561 --> 00:02:58,722
AI 学会的第一件事，可能是找捷径。
The first thing AI learns may be how to find a shortcut.

58
00:02:58,922 --> 00:03:01,642
第五件，AI 写的假漏洞报告太多，
Fifth, there were so many bogus AI-written bug reports

59
00:03:01,662 --> 00:03:04,442
谷歌干脆把一个赏金计划停了一部分。
that Google paused part of a bounty program.

60
00:03:04,462 --> 00:03:07,132
IT之家报道，从 10 月 1 日起，
IT Home reports that from October 1,

61
00:03:07,152 --> 00:03:11,052
谷歌的开源软件漏洞奖励计划不再接收产品漏洞。
Google's Open Source Software Vulnerability Reward Program stopped taking product bugs.

62
00:03:11,072 --> 00:03:13,552
原因是收到了数以千计的劣质报告，
The reason: thousands of low-quality reports,

63
00:03:13,572 --> 00:03:16,022
很多是 AI 幻觉编出来的漏洞。
many describing bugs that AI simply hallucinated.

64
00:03:16,042 --> 00:03:19,684
工程师得一条条去查，真问题反而被耽误了。
Engineers had to check each one, and real issues got delayed.

65
00:03:19,704 --> 00:03:21,855
10 月 1 日以前交的报告不受影响，
Reports filed before October 1 aren't affected,

66
00:03:21,875 --> 00:03:24,925
部分谷歌云的仓库还能走云漏洞计划。
and some Google Cloud repos can still go through the Cloud VRP.

67
00:03:24,945 --> 00:03:29,645
谷歌说会重新调整这个计划，2027 年第一季度给出新进展。
Google says it will rework the program and give an update in the first quarter of 2027.

68
00:03:29,665 --> 00:03:33,070
AI 能帮人找漏洞，也能帮人造垃圾。
AI can help find bugs, and it can also help mass-produce junk.

69
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:35,490
第六件，往 COSMIC 交代码，
Sixth, if you send code to COSMIC now,

70
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:38,650
现在得先发誓：一行都不是 AI 写的。
you have to promise none of it was written by AI.

71
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:41,425
COSMIC 是 System76 用 Rust 写的 Linux 桌面。
COSMIC is a Linux desktop System76 builds in Rust.

72
00:03:41,445 --> 00:03:45,085
Linuxiac 10 月 2 日报道，它改了 PR 模板。
Linuxiac reported on October 2 that it changed its PR template.

73
00:03:45,105 --> 00:03:48,718
提交时要勾一项：没有放任何大模型生成的内容。
Contributors must tick a box saying they included no LLM-generated content.

74
00:03:48,738 --> 00:03:51,504
代码、注释、PR 描述都算在内。
That covers code, comments and PR descriptions.

75
00:03:51,524 --> 00:03:54,374
为什么？System76 的 Jeremy Soller 说，
Why? Jeremy Soller of System76 says

76
00:03:54,394 --> 00:03:56,994
新手用大模型交的 PR 越来越多，
more first-timers are sending LLM-made PRs,

77
00:03:57,014 --> 00:03:59,664
大多没规划，很少被采纳。
mostly unplanned and rarely accepted.

78
00:03:59,684 --> 00:04:01,864
他们也说了，并不反对 AI 工具，
They also say they're fine with AI tools in general;

79
00:04:01,884 --> 00:04:04,249
就是想让审核忙得过来。
they just want reviews to stay manageable.

80
00:04:04,269 --> 00:04:08,239
代码能一键生成，审核的人可没法一键复制。
Code can be generated in one click. Reviewers can't.

81
00:04:08,439 --> 00:04:11,170
第七件，你打字时输入法猜下一个词，
Seventh, when you type, your keyboard guesses the next word.

82
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:13,740
以前一个模型要训练一到两个月。
One such model used to take one to two months to train.

83
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,910
10 月 2 日，谷歌研究院发文，
On October 2, Google Research announced

84
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:18,990
说给 Gboard 换了一套新的联邦学习系统。
a new federated learning system for Gboard.

85
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:20,345
以前是在手机上算，
Before, the computing happened on phones,

86
00:04:20,365 --> 00:04:23,180
受限于手机有没有空、算力够不够。
limited by whether they were free and how much power they had.

87
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:25,081
现在数据加密后传到服务器，
Now the data is encrypted and sent to servers,

88
00:04:25,101 --> 00:04:26,821
在可信执行环境里算，
processed inside trusted execution environments,

89
00:04:26,841 --> 00:04:29,311
也就是一块别人看不到的隔离区。
sealed-off zones no one else can see into.

90
00:04:29,331 --> 00:04:30,891
服务器上能跑什么程序，
What may run on those servers

91
00:04:30,911 --> 00:04:33,751
规则公开写在一个叫 Rekor 的透明日志里，
is published in a public log called Rekor,

92
00:04:33,771 --> 00:04:35,021
外人可以查。
so outsiders can check.

93
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:38,742
Gboard 的英语和日语下一词预测模型已经用上了，
Gboard's English and Japanese next-word prediction models already use it,

94
00:04:38,762 --> 00:04:40,921
隐私更强，准确率也更高。
with stronger privacy and better accuracy.

95
00:04:40,941 --> 00:04:45,252
测试里，一个英语模型训练了 5000 轮，每轮 6500 台设备。
In one test, an English model trained for 5000 rounds with 6500 devices per round.

96
00:04:45,272 --> 00:04:48,747
隐私光靠一句保证不够，得能让人去查。
A privacy promise alone isn't enough. People need to be able to check.

97
00:04:48,947 --> 00:04:53,123
最后一件，一个 AI 智能体在熟悉的环境里拿了 97.1%，
Last one: an AI agent scored 97.1 percent in a familiar setting.

98
00:04:53,143 --> 00:04:55,783
换个陌生环境，0 分。
In an unfamiliar one, 0.

99
00:04:55,803 --> 00:04:58,298
这是 The Decoder 10 月 4 日报道里举的例子，
That's an example from a report by The Decoder on October 4,

100
00:04:58,318 --> 00:05:00,228
说的是 AI 会死记考题。
about AI memorizing its tests.

101
00:05:00,248 --> 00:05:04,378
现在很多智能体会自己改自己的提示词、工具和流程，
Many agents now edit their own prompts, tools and workflows,

102
00:05:04,398 --> 00:05:05,738
越改分越高。
and their scores keep rising.

103
00:05:05,758 --> 00:05:08,279
但改着改着就变成了针对题目作弊，
But over time, the edits turn into tailoring for the test,

104
00:05:08,299 --> 00:05:10,174
换一套题就不灵了。
and they fall apart on new tasks.

105
00:05:10,194 --> 00:05:13,954
谷歌云 AI 研究团队联合几所大学，提出了 RRSI。
Google Cloud AI Research and several universities proposed RRSI.

106
00:05:13,974 --> 00:05:17,214
做法是两条：每轮能改的地方越来越少，
Two rules: fewer edits allowed each round,

107
00:05:17,234 --> 00:05:20,734
再派一个评审员，拦下只针对某道题的改动。
and a critic that blocks changes aimed at specific benchmarks.

108
00:05:20,754 --> 00:05:23,254
结果在练过的题上最多涨 14.1 分，
It gained up to 14.1 points on the tasks it trained on

109
00:05:23,274 --> 00:05:26,354
五个没见过的测试上最多涨 4.7 分，
and up to 4.7 on five unseen benchmarks,

110
00:05:26,374 --> 00:05:28,084
还少用约 30% 的 token。
using about 30 percent fewer tokens.

111
00:05:28,104 --> 00:05:32,724
论文 9 月 21 日就挂到了 arXiv 上，目前还是预印本。
The paper went up on arXiv on September 21 and is still a preprint.

112
00:05:32,744 --> 00:05:35,880
会考试不难，难的是换张卷子还会。
Passing a test is easy. Passing a new one is the hard part.

113
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,840
今天就这些，来源都在简介里。
That's all for today. Sources are in the description.

114
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:42,319
国庆假期过半，好好休息，我们明天见。
The National Day holiday is half over. Get some rest, and see you tomorrow.
